WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:03.480
Sho!

00:05.020 --> 00:06.560
We meet again.

00:08.920 --> 00:10.160
Who are you?

00:10.820 --> 00:11.730
Big brother?

00:19.300 --> 00:21.890
Was that... an Adolla Link?

00:22.370 --> 00:23.380
Was I...

00:26.760 --> 00:30.590
What happened after that? My memories are...

00:33.030 --> 00:34.630
Haumea said...

00:35.080 --> 00:39.030
That's right. We will turn this planet 
into a flaming star once again.

00:39.030 --> 00:41.050
That is our mission.

00:43.290 --> 00:46.980
But then I met my brother, my only family,

00:47.400 --> 00:51.490
and when I did, I felt a warmth 
I've never felt before.

00:52.010 --> 00:55.550
Flames. Burning. Melting.

00:55.550 --> 00:58.860
It felt so different from 
fires that engulf everything.

01:01.970 --> 01:05.100
I must see my brother again.

01:08.830 --> 01:11.960
<i>I can't let any of the Guardians 
sense what I'm doing.</i>

01:11.960 --> 01:13.850
Sho! 'Sup?

01:14.430 --> 01:17.000
As unfriendly as ever, I see.

01:17.000 --> 01:18.170
Where's Haumea?

01:18.170 --> 01:20.140
She's locked herself in that room again.

01:21.150 --> 01:23.220
<i>This girl can see the future.</i>

01:23.220 --> 01:25.510
<i>She may be able to pick up on something.</i>

01:25.510 --> 01:28.510
<i>I don't want to stay here 
too long. I'll go that way.</i>

01:29.180 --> 01:31.950
<i>If Haumea is preoccupied 
with all that right now,</i>

01:31.950 --> 01:33.780
<i>this is my chance to escape to the Nether.</i>

01:34.070 --> 01:36.980
Good day, Third Pillar Sho-kun.

01:37.360 --> 01:38.970
Sister Sumire.

01:38.970 --> 01:42.170
Oh? Has something about you changed a bit?

01:42.170 --> 01:43.400
What are you talking about?

01:44.710 --> 01:47.560
<i>I don't want to stay near 
this old lady for long.</i>

01:48.050 --> 01:49.250
<i>I'll go that way.</i>

01:49.250 --> 01:52.340
Hey, Sho! You're as short as ever today.

01:52.340 --> 01:55.350
<i>Why is it that at times like this 
I run into more people than usual?</i>

01:55.350 --> 01:57.700
<i>Charon is Haumea's Guardian.</i>

01:57.700 --> 02:00.660
<i>It would be bad if he found me 
out. I don't want to stay here.</i>

02:00.660 --> 02:01.960
<i>I'll go that way.</i>

02:03.670 --> 02:04.640
Captain.

02:05.490 --> 02:07.110
<i>Who is it now?</i>

02:07.500 --> 02:09.710
Arrow? What is it?

02:09.710 --> 02:12.730
The last mass before the Great 
Cataclysm is nearly upon us.

02:12.730 --> 02:14.110
If I may ask, where are you going?

02:14.400 --> 02:17.820
<i>Oh. So that's why there 
are so many people here.</i>

02:18.180 --> 02:19.820
Is something wrong?

02:21.260 --> 02:23.780
<i>There may indeed be 
something wrong with me.</i>

02:24.090 --> 02:25.930
<i>What will meeting my brother accomplish?</i>

02:25.930 --> 02:29.390
<i>Is there something there, 
something separate from my duty?</i>

02:29.390 --> 02:34.120
<i>Even if I were to gain my 
freedom, what would I do?</i>

02:34.420 --> 02:37.300
We will be late for the mass. We should go.

02:37.970 --> 02:39.310
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

02:39.580 --> 02:41.380
<i>My brother went all the way to the Nether.</i>

02:41.930 --> 02:45.100
<i>It isn't that I especially want to see him.</i>

02:45.100 --> 02:48.920
<i>But I can't just ignore these feelings.</i>

02:53.220 --> 02:54.190
Captain.

02:55.510 --> 02:57.190
Lead me outside.

02:57.730 --> 02:59.650
If you resist, I'll kill you.

03:01.880 --> 03:03.820
I am a Guardian.

03:03.820 --> 03:06.340
I would never betray you, Captain.

03:07.100 --> 03:08.900
What do you mean?

03:08.900 --> 03:13.600
Wherever you may go, 
it is my duty to protect you.

03:13.600 --> 03:15.660
Let there be no question of that.

03:16.710 --> 03:20.900
What if I told you that duty 
was no longer necessary?

03:22.570 --> 03:24.470
<i>Arrow is like me.</i>

03:25.130 --> 03:30.590
<i>We act because of duty and don't 
know what to do outside of it.</i>

03:31.640 --> 03:37.780
You and I act according to the Evangelist's 
will. We live to fulfill our duty.

03:38.040 --> 03:40.400
But I've discovered something else I must do.

03:40.720 --> 03:44.580
You should abandon all this and 
act according to your own will, too.

03:45.030 --> 03:47.720
My duty is nothing like that.

03:47.720 --> 03:48.700
And the difference is?

03:50.900 --> 03:54.370
Fulfilling my duty is an act of my own will.

03:55.060 --> 03:57.820
Your safety is my happiness.

03:58.290 --> 04:02.990
Serving you is my reason 
for living, my everything.

04:03.710 --> 04:07.340
Were I to abandon my duty,
I would have no reason to live.

04:08.010 --> 04:10.840
I am a single arrow that 
serves to protect you.

04:10.840 --> 04:14.890
Once an arrow is loosed,
it can never be called back.

04:21.630 --> 04:23.810
Wherever you go, I shall accompany you.

04:23.810 --> 04:25.140
There's no need.

04:34.600 --> 04:36.950
I'm telling you not to follow me.

04:36.950 --> 04:39.830
Then how much distance should 
I maintain between us?

04:39.830 --> 04:42.700
Far enough that you can't see me at all.

04:42.700 --> 04:46.520
In that case, I shall maintain my 
absolute farthest firing distance.

04:47.310 --> 04:48.590
Do as you like.

04:48.590 --> 04:49.390
Sir!

06:01.210 --> 06:07.970
<b>Fire Force</b>

06:08.090 --> 06:11.970
<b>Fire Force</b>

06:08.300 --> 06:11.970
<b>Chapter 3</b>

06:29.460 --> 06:30.400
It's morning?

06:31.250 --> 06:34.450
I feel like I saw Sho.

06:34.450 --> 06:36.500
Did I trigger an Adolla Link?

06:36.950 --> 06:39.210
Good morning, Shinra-san!

06:39.210 --> 06:41.520
Sister! Good morning!

06:41.520 --> 06:43.890
Were you able to sleep properly, 
lying in a spot like that?

06:43.890 --> 06:46.000
Yes! I feel like I got too much sleep, actually!

06:46.000 --> 06:46.670
My!

06:47.030 --> 06:51.390
Maki-san said we'll have a meeting 
when the captain returns,

06:51.390 --> 06:53.800
so it'd probably be best to wake up fully now.

06:53.800 --> 06:56.540
Did Captain Obi go somewhere?

06:56.540 --> 06:59.310
Yes, he went somewhere early this morning.

06:59.310 --> 06:59.970
Oh...

07:00.360 --> 07:02.580
Well, if you'll excuse me.

07:02.580 --> 07:03.310
Of course!

07:03.800 --> 07:05.270
Thank you!

07:08.810 --> 07:12.480
<i>Amaterasu is operating 
at normal capacity today.</i>

07:18.080 --> 07:21.080
<b>Episode 10
"Advent"</b>

07:21.080 --> 07:24.540
<b>Asakusa</b>

07:21.080 --> 07:24.540
<b>Kaminarimon</b>

07:22.560 --> 07:26.410
We will now begin an emergency meeting 
of Special Fire Force Company 8.

07:26.860 --> 07:30.430
As you know, the empire has joined 
forces with the White Clad,

07:30.430 --> 07:34.130
and we of the 8th have 
been branded as traitors.

07:34.480 --> 07:38.680
We were working at strengthening our ties 
with various powers within the empire,

07:39.140 --> 07:40.600
but given the current circumstances,

07:40.600 --> 07:44.770
obtaining the aid of the Holy Sol 
Temple, including the 1st, Haijima,

07:44.770 --> 07:46.530
or the army will be difficult.

07:46.900 --> 07:50.110
If we could at least get the 
Imperial Army to act...

07:50.340 --> 07:55.230
Couldn't you ask General Oze? 
He's your father, isn't he?

07:55.230 --> 08:00.050
Since I quit the army, he hates 
the 8th and Lieutenant Hinawa,

08:00.050 --> 08:02.330
so he'd just end up telling me to come home.

08:02.330 --> 08:05.790
And there's one more thing we 
got a report about yesterday.

08:06.160 --> 08:09.090
The Great Cataclysm is happening soon.

08:09.750 --> 08:12.970
The Great Cataclysm?
Where'd we get that information from?

08:12.970 --> 08:14.430
From me.

08:14.430 --> 08:16.110
Captain Hibana?

08:16.110 --> 08:17.280
Big sister?

08:21.790 --> 08:23.010
Iris.

08:23.260 --> 08:26.400
Have you noticed anything 
unusual with your health?

08:27.000 --> 08:29.280
No, nothing in particular.

08:29.280 --> 08:30.330
I see.

08:30.820 --> 08:33.510
The more important question is,
why are you here?

08:33.510 --> 08:35.200
To bring you this.

08:35.200 --> 08:41.160
<b>St. Raffles Convent
Investigation Report</b>

08:35.510 --> 08:39.350
My report on the Great Cataclysm 
and spontaneous human combustion.

08:39.350 --> 08:40.520
I finished writing it.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.170
Thank you for—

08:44.110 --> 08:44.840
Hey!

08:44.840 --> 08:47.490
It's more important for him 
to read it than for me to.

08:50.750 --> 08:54.970
Captain Hibana is the 
8th's first collaborator.

08:54.970 --> 08:58.410
Circumstances being what they are,
thanks for joining us.

08:58.410 --> 09:01.050
I am not assisting the 8th!

09:01.050 --> 09:05.680
But it isn't as if I hate everyone in the 8th.

09:05.680 --> 09:07.840
Right, Shinra?

09:08.590 --> 09:11.020
Thank you for doing this for the 8th!

09:11.020 --> 09:12.870
Is Kusakabe doing that on purpose?

09:12.870 --> 09:15.230
And to think he's usually 
got pretty good instincts.

09:15.230 --> 09:20.190
But I think an older man would suit 
you much better than a younger man.

09:20.190 --> 09:21.960
Iris, where'd that come from?

09:21.960 --> 09:24.260
For example, what about Captain Obi?

09:24.260 --> 09:28.000
Me? I'd be a weird choice, wouldn't I?
Our ages are much too far apart.

09:28.000 --> 09:29.050
Do you think so?

09:29.050 --> 09:32.190
These days, no one cares 
much about an age gap.

09:32.190 --> 09:34.450
In that case, what about Lieutenant Hinawa?

09:34.450 --> 09:37.070
W-Wouldn't Lieutenant Hinawa
would be an odd choice?

09:37.070 --> 09:38.440
Why are you panicking all of a sudden?

09:38.440 --> 09:40.570
Panic?! Who's panicking?!

09:38.810 --> 09:42.080
Hey! Stop trying to force people on me.

09:42.810 --> 09:46.770
Also, I think someone like Tamaki-san 
would suit Shinra-san better.

09:46.000 --> 09:46.770
What?!

09:46.770 --> 09:49.340
Iris! Why would you stick 
me with a guy like him?!

09:49.340 --> 09:52.400
Don't act like you're superior, cat.
I'm the one saying no to you.

09:52.400 --> 09:54.640
I prefer women like the sister!

09:54.640 --> 09:56.900
Ugh, you're so gross.
I'm a sister too, you know!

09:56.900 --> 09:59.990
Yes, I like you very much, too, Shinra-san!

10:00.780 --> 10:01.930
How gross can you be?

10:01.930 --> 10:04.840
And I'd make a way better match 
for you than Iris would, anyway!

10:04.840 --> 10:06.480
What?! Now who's being gross?

10:06.480 --> 10:09.100
The sister smiles like an 
angel as she stirs up chaos.

10:09.100 --> 10:10.720
Innocent types are scary.

10:11.650 --> 10:15.050
Are you guys from Tokyo always fighting?

10:16.230 --> 10:18.820
Lushan Mole Whack!

10:18.550 --> 10:20.800
<b>Lushan Mole Whack</b>

10:20.800 --> 10:22.380
It talks?

10:23.280 --> 10:24.630
A mole?

10:25.780 --> 10:27.140
Scop?

10:27.600 --> 10:29.460
Shinra!

10:29.460 --> 10:31.880
Scop! What're you doing here?

10:31.880 --> 10:34.350
I worked myself really hard to get to Tokyo!

10:34.920 --> 10:38.390
First, there was the journey 
from the Oasis to the harbor.

10:38.390 --> 10:40.960
I ran into a Hell Hound that had survived!

10:40.960 --> 10:44.360
I thought I was done for, 
but then I had an epiphany!

10:44.360 --> 10:47.160
The area where I'm most 
effective is underground!

10:47.960 --> 10:51.480
Once I realized that,
I immediately dug down!

10:53.460 --> 10:56.900
But that Hell Hound just wouldn't give up.

10:56.900 --> 11:00.330
It just kept following me above ground.

11:00.600 --> 11:05.660
There was no end in sight. In fact, 
I was the one at a disadvantage.

11:05.660 --> 11:07.600
When I grew tired from tunneling,

11:07.600 --> 11:11.390
the Hell Hound would dig 
a hole to try to kill me!

11:11.730 --> 11:15.350
It was a terrifying creature, and we 
were locked in a battle of endurance.

11:15.630 --> 11:17.500
But the outcome was clear to see.

11:17.500 --> 11:22.450
I was tunneling, so I'd grow tired faster 
than the thing just walking along the ground.

11:22.450 --> 11:24.950
If I was going to challenge it, 
sooner would be better than later.

11:24.950 --> 11:27.240
I'd do it while I still had strength!

11:27.240 --> 11:30.540
What I unleashed in that moment 
was what you just saw...

11:30.540 --> 11:33.300
Lushan Mole Whack!

11:32.960 --> 11:40.380
<b>Lushan Mole Whack</b>

11:34.990 --> 11:36.240
Allow me to explain.

11:36.240 --> 11:40.390
The Lushan Mole Whack focuses all 
digging power into my right arm

11:40.390 --> 11:43.640
and makes the fur all over 
my body stand on end.

11:43.640 --> 11:46.630
This creates a single knockout blow!

11:47.330 --> 11:50.540
The one who was most surprised 
was none other than myself.

11:50.200 --> 11:53.550
Um, sorry. Can I ask something, Scop?

11:50.540 --> 11:54.100
Before, when I promised Shinra that 
I'd dig a thousand holes a day, I—

11:54.840 --> 11:59.300
That's a really interesting story,
but that's not what I want to know right now.

11:59.300 --> 12:01.520
What brought you all the way here?

12:01.520 --> 12:02.850
What brought me?

12:02.850 --> 12:04.230
Yes. What brought you?

12:06.410 --> 12:08.710
What brought me here, you ask?

12:09.470 --> 12:13.130
Do not be shocked when 
I tell you what brought me!

12:13.130 --> 12:15.930
The Hell Hound that collapsed 
after being struck

12:15.930 --> 12:18.810
with my Lushan Mole Whack 
stood and looked at me.

12:18.810 --> 12:23.210
The Lushan Mole Whack had brought 
me both victory and friendship.

12:23.720 --> 12:27.800
The Hell Hound carried me on its 
back all the way to the harbor.

12:27.800 --> 12:32.390
So if you ask what brought me,
then I say a Hell Hound brought me!

12:32.690 --> 12:37.360
I had to find my way to the harbor 
and board a ship headed for Tokyo.

12:37.360 --> 12:39.240
The Hell Hound was fast.

12:39.240 --> 12:44.650
I made it safely to the harbor,
but that meant we had to part ways.

12:44.650 --> 12:46.740
Still, I had no time to be sad.

12:46.740 --> 12:50.040
I held back my tears and found 
a ship headed for Tokyo.

12:50.040 --> 12:54.450
I climbed into one of the cardboard boxes 
with the Noto label packed with potatoes.

12:54.780 --> 12:59.450
And since it was very packed indeed, 
I had to eat a little in order to fit inside.

12:59.450 --> 13:03.040
I'm sorry, Juggernaut. 
It was all in the line of duty.

13:04.880 --> 13:10.670
The voyage went smoothly, and by the time we 
reached Tokyo, I'd eaten all the potatoes!

13:10.670 --> 13:12.660
I'm sorry, Juggernaut.

13:13.050 --> 13:17.140
But I heard someone say, 
"Damn it! Rats got to this box!"

13:17.140 --> 13:20.250
Rats? What an insolent fellow. Me? A rat?

13:20.250 --> 13:23.900
Why would he call me a rat, of all things?

13:23.900 --> 13:25.370
It was unforgivable.

13:25.370 --> 13:29.420
Why would he think that my 
crimes were those of a rat?

13:29.420 --> 13:30.570
Unforgivable!

13:30.570 --> 13:34.100
No matter how you look at me, I am no—

13:36.810 --> 13:41.480
What I saw in the mirror 
was neither mole nor rat.

13:42.180 --> 13:43.350
It was a potato.

13:44.500 --> 13:47.170
Neo Knight Shot!

13:51.170 --> 13:54.370
Wh-Wh-What brought that on out of the blue?

13:54.370 --> 13:55.900
Well done, Arthur.

13:55.900 --> 13:58.600
It was a little forceful, 
but good job stopping him.

13:58.600 --> 14:01.610
You shouldn't eat other people's 
potatoes without permission!

14:01.610 --> 14:04.140
That's right, mole-san! Látom!

14:04.140 --> 14:05.430
That's the problem?

14:05.430 --> 14:07.900
I read the report, but...

14:07.900 --> 14:10.570
Yeah. He really is a talking mole.

14:10.570 --> 14:14.860
I thought they'd gotten high on underground
gas and suffered auditory hallucinations.

14:14.860 --> 14:16.700
Give him to me!

14:14.950 --> 14:15.330
<b>SNATCH</b>

14:16.700 --> 14:20.460
Scop, what did you come to Tokyo to do?

14:20.460 --> 14:25.020
That's right! Shinra, I came here to tell you

14:25.020 --> 14:26.930
the lady in black's last words.

14:27.420 --> 14:30.920
I'm going to tell you about what's going 
to happen in the Great Cataclysm.

14:31.970 --> 14:34.970
<b>Fire Force</b>

14:31.970 --> 14:34.970
<b>Chapter 3</b>

14:34.970 --> 14:37.980
<b>Fire Force</b>

14:34.970 --> 14:37.980
<b>Chapter 3</b>

14:39.190 --> 14:41.310
Burn the land.

14:41.630 --> 14:45.060
May we all follow the path 
shown to us by the Evangelist.

14:45.780 --> 14:47.270
Látom.

14:48.170 --> 14:50.180
The Third Pillar isn't here.

14:50.180 --> 14:51.960
Sho has run away.

14:51.960 --> 14:52.970
Sho-kun did what?

14:52.970 --> 14:55.490
It isn't a problem. Let him do as he likes.

14:55.490 --> 15:00.560
Until now, we have simply assembled the 
Pillars in the hopes of awakening Adolla Bursts.

15:00.560 --> 15:02.160
Oh. Really?

15:02.420 --> 15:07.440
No matter where the Pillars may be, 
they can no longer escape Adolla.

15:07.440 --> 15:09.660
The Pillars will become supports 
that connect to Adolla,

15:09.660 --> 15:11.840
and the Great Cataclysm is about to begin.

15:13.080 --> 15:16.630
Lots of people are going to die this time, 
too, right? I can't wait to see it!

15:16.630 --> 15:17.770
I'm so excited!

15:18.180 --> 15:19.520
Nothing could be better!

15:19.520 --> 15:24.510
My lady Inca, until the day comes that you 
keel over, I, Ritsu, shall protect you.

15:24.510 --> 15:27.220
You might die before me, though.

15:27.220 --> 15:31.080
I can't wait to see! It's a contest 
to see which of us dies first, okay?

15:32.010 --> 15:34.140
The time has come, then?

15:34.600 --> 15:36.080
I've waited a long time,

15:36.080 --> 15:38.850
but now I can finally fulfill my purpose.

15:39.390 --> 15:40.540
So you've come,

15:40.920 --> 15:43.750
Great Cataclysm Execution Officer Faerie.

15:44.260 --> 15:47.370
The Guardian with no Pillar to protect?

15:47.370 --> 15:49.800
Why is this garbage fluttering around?

15:49.800 --> 15:53.230
There is no one in this 
world who can defeat you.

15:53.740 --> 15:57.920
But after the cataclysm I awaken,
nothing will remain.

15:58.660 --> 15:59.750
Including you.

16:02.240 --> 16:04.540
Haumea, how does it look?

16:04.540 --> 16:05.600
Well...

16:06.070 --> 16:09.200
Don't you dare look down on me!
You can go ahead and die!

16:09.200 --> 16:10.860
Die! This is your fault!

16:10.860 --> 16:13.760
Don't try to pull that on me!
Why don't you just die?

16:27.420 --> 16:30.850
By the Evangelist's orders, 
we shall begin the mass!

16:32.150 --> 16:33.930
What's this? What's this?

16:33.930 --> 16:35.890
You won't listen to my tale 
of adventure, but you—

16:35.890 --> 16:36.850
Just tell us.

16:37.230 --> 16:40.250
Well, okay. That's why I came, after all.

16:41.170 --> 16:43.680
She was already starting to disappear.

16:43.970 --> 16:46.460
She said that the Great 
Cataclysm was imminent.

16:46.760 --> 16:50.280
One of the primary reasons that 
the last Great Cataclysm failed

16:50.280 --> 16:54.690
was because pi hadn't been calculated 
yet. That's what she told me.

16:54.690 --> 16:58.460
That's why the Evangelist increased 
the level of humanity's civilization

16:58.460 --> 17:02.050
and had it progress to an era 
when pi would be calculated.

17:02.660 --> 17:06.960
My ancestor built Amaterasu 
and left that key.

17:07.430 --> 17:12.130
This is just a hypothesis, but if there's 
a connection between Amaterasu and pi,

17:12.130 --> 17:14.750
then maybe the key that Giovanni stole

17:14.750 --> 17:17.570
was the key to deciphering pi.

17:17.570 --> 17:18.690
I see.

17:18.980 --> 17:22.530
Vulcan-kun's ancestor deciphered pi.

17:22.530 --> 17:28.340
And according to Captain Hibana's report, 
the eight Pillars are all in place.

17:28.340 --> 17:30.400
That's what she said, too.

17:30.770 --> 17:35.230
Which means everything needed for the 
next Great Cataclysm is already in place.

17:35.660 --> 17:38.440
This world and Adolla will become one...

17:38.440 --> 17:40.320
and this planet will burn.

17:42.190 --> 17:46.180
It's true that this situation isn't 
good, but don't look so depressed.

17:46.750 --> 17:49.450
It's not all bad news.

17:49.450 --> 17:53.210
By the way, Captain, where 
did you go this morning?

17:53.210 --> 17:54.450
It's dangerous for you.

17:54.450 --> 17:56.680
I went to meet with a few people.

17:56.680 --> 17:58.430
<b>Café</b>

17:56.680 --> 17:58.430
<b>Fig</b>

18:01.540 --> 18:03.350
What's going on, Obi?

18:03.350 --> 18:06.630
I'm sorry for the roundabout methods.

18:06.630 --> 18:09.080
We're seen as traitors right now.

18:09.080 --> 18:11.690
I know that. What's so urgent?

18:12.030 --> 18:14.800
You're aware that the 
Great Cataclysm is near?

18:15.720 --> 18:16.820
What of it?

18:17.350 --> 18:20.970
I'd like to know what the 2nd 
sees of the Empire's movements.

18:20.970 --> 18:22.580
I want to know if you'll help us.

18:22.580 --> 18:25.310
And for that, you exposed 
yourself to this danger?

18:26.030 --> 18:28.760
You didn't think I'd anonymously report you?

18:28.760 --> 18:30.850
I did it because of the danger.

18:30.850 --> 18:34.280
I'm the boss. That means I'm 
the one who has to do this.

18:35.190 --> 18:36.550
Yes, well...

18:36.550 --> 18:39.760
I know you don't lie or prevaricate.

18:39.760 --> 18:43.020
That's why your soldiers 
and allies follow you.

18:43.780 --> 18:46.840
But the empire and Imperial Army 
aren't so different from you.

18:46.840 --> 18:49.960
Unless something happens, they can't act.

18:49.960 --> 18:52.270
Orders from above are absolute.

18:52.270 --> 18:54.530
I realize that.

18:54.530 --> 18:57.600
You can't openly offer the 
8th any assistance, right?

18:57.600 --> 19:02.280
But, sir, I ask that you and the 2nd 
be as prepared as you possibly can be.

19:02.280 --> 19:05.240
Prepared? Prepared for what, exactly?

19:05.790 --> 19:07.320
For anything.

19:08.230 --> 19:12.720
Go. Army patrols will be in this area soon.

19:16.750 --> 19:19.240
I was planning to go see you myself.

19:19.600 --> 19:22.280
I never imagined you'd 
come and see me directly.

19:24.720 --> 19:28.320
The 4th is prepared to support 
the 8th with everything we have.

19:28.930 --> 19:30.550
An emergency situation is no time

19:30.550 --> 19:33.010
to be talking about the importance 
of the empire's orders.

19:33.600 --> 19:36.410
It's possible that you'll 
be charged with treason.

19:36.690 --> 19:39.430
Captain Hague always regretted

19:39.430 --> 19:42.640
that it's an ironclad rule 
that fire soldiers can't act

19:42.640 --> 19:44.510
until a fire has broken out.

19:44.980 --> 19:48.750
Back when you were stripped of your honors, 
and that second time you defied orders...

19:49.120 --> 19:52.040
Both times, you acted to save human lives.

19:52.340 --> 19:53.740
That's who you are.

19:54.250 --> 19:55.870
This charge of treason

19:55.870 --> 19:59.710
must also be the result of you taking 
action to put others' lives first.

20:00.090 --> 20:03.600
A fire soldier's duty is to 
protect lives and property.

20:04.890 --> 20:06.220
I will help you.

20:07.410 --> 20:10.630
Thank you, Captain Pan. I'm counting on you.

20:15.850 --> 20:18.060
It's feeding time! Koi, fall in!

20:18.060 --> 20:20.590
Um, please stop. You'll attract attention.

20:20.590 --> 20:23.570
Fire soldiers don't sneak around, so...

20:24.040 --> 20:25.160
I wasn't thinking.

20:27.810 --> 20:30.210
So the 4th decided to ally with us?

20:30.210 --> 20:36.160
Yes, and Captain Honda of the 2nd 
will help us as a private individual.

20:36.440 --> 20:40.000
But we don't know what will 
happen in the Great Cataclysm.

20:40.000 --> 20:43.620
To be honest, I can't say our 
forces are sufficient yet.

20:43.620 --> 20:44.950
You're right.

20:44.950 --> 20:47.440
But as long as we don't give up hope,

20:47.440 --> 20:49.600
I know there are people 
out there who will help us.

20:50.800 --> 20:53.860
We are going to stop the 
Great Cataclysm in its tracks!

20:53.860 --> 20:55.170
Yes, sir!

20:55.800 --> 20:57.420
All right, we have to get ready.

20:57.420 --> 20:58.980
Oh! It's happening again!

20:58.980 --> 21:00.900
Scop? What is it?

21:00.900 --> 21:02.620
On my way here to Tokyo,

21:02.620 --> 21:06.370
I felt a weird energy flow 
through the ground many times.

21:06.370 --> 21:07.950
A weird energy?

21:07.950 --> 21:09.910
Yes. I felt it again just now.

21:09.910 --> 21:14.460
When I followed it before, I ended 
up at a room with pillars in it.

21:15.280 --> 21:20.570
There was a strange old lady... 
and that lady there, too.

21:21.360 --> 21:23.490
You were in that documents room?

21:23.990 --> 21:27.170
Could it be that this 
weird energy you feel...

21:27.170 --> 21:29.900
and the frequent mysterious 
earthquakes of late...

21:30.450 --> 21:33.440
are both caused by Sister Sumire?

21:33.440 --> 21:37.720
They're causing earthquakes with the 
intent of getting something started.

21:38.140 --> 21:42.120
Bring destruction by fire to this world.

21:42.120 --> 21:45.440
The humans above ground are frightened.

21:45.440 --> 21:47.700
Let us show them ruin by fire.

21:47.700 --> 21:49.010
Sumire.

21:49.010 --> 21:49.880
Yes.

22:01.170 --> 22:02.300
Another earthquake!

22:02.300 --> 22:03.130
It's a big one!

22:03.130 --> 22:05.690
This shaking is not natural!

22:08.160 --> 22:09.210
What was that?

22:09.210 --> 22:10.700
There was a sound...

22:10.700 --> 22:12.200
Hey! Th-This is...

22:12.200 --> 22:13.500
Hey! Wait! Stop!

22:16.760 --> 22:18.490
Hey, look!

22:18.490 --> 22:21.110
What is that?! What's going on?!

22:38.000 --> 22:42.000
<b>To Be Continued</b>

24:11.930 --> 24:13.430
<b>Fire Force Chapter 3</b>

24:12.420 --> 24:14.100
Who is this guy?

24:13.250 --> 24:17.010
Being huge and powerful isn't 
very endearing, is it?

24:13.430 --> 24:14.760
<b>Next Time</b>

24:15.900 --> 24:19.340
The enemy is on the water. Laying them 
to rest will require flight ability.

24:18.160 --> 24:20.830
Don't give up! Keep firing!

24:19.480 --> 24:22.060
The Great Cataclysm has begun.

24:22.060 --> 24:24.040
Next time, "The Great Kaiju Battlefront."

24:22.060 --> 24:26.930
<b>Episode 11</b>

24:22.060 --> 24:26.930
<b>The Great Kaiju Battlefront</b>

24:24.040 --> 24:26.630
Return to the great flame of fire. Látom.
